cff-version: 1.2.0
version: 0.0.8
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the original
  Timeless Timing Attacks paper.
title: >-
  tturl: Timeless timing and request races over HTTP/2
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Steven
    given-names: Justin
    affiliation: Tanto Security
contact:
  - name: Tanto Security
    email: research@tantosec.com
    website: https://tantosec.com
abstract: >-
  tturl is an HTTP/2 CLI for finding tiny timing differences and winning
  request races through batch release and relative response arrival order. The
  repository also provides the reusable tth2 batch-release engine,
  domain-free statistical primitives in stats, and the internal ranking
  subsystem behind tturl detect.
repository-code: https://github.com/tantosec/tturl
keywords:
  - timing attacks
  - side channels
  - HTTP/2
  - request races
  - Go
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    authors:
      - family-names: Van Goethem
        given-names: Tom
      - family-names: Pöpper
        given-names: Christina
      - family-names: Joosen
        given-names: Wouter
      - family-names: Vanhoef
        given-names: Mathy
    title: >-
      Timeless Timing Attacks: Exploiting Concurrency to Leak Secrets over
      Remote Connections
    collection-title: 29th USENIX Security Symposium (USENIX Security 20)
    year: 2020
    month: 8
    start: 1985
    end: 2002
    publisher:
      name: USENIX Association
    url: >-
      https://www.usenix.org/conference/usenixsecurity20/presentation/van-goethem
    scope: Introduces the timeless timing attack technique implemented here.
